      "writtenOn": "2026-04-23T08:59:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if we could use a `BindGroupLayout` created reentrantly: we have support for texture bindings with [`kInputAttachmentDim`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/PipelineLayout.cpp;drc\u003d01f3fea318f80b5541e1d5eb8dfeb174820926be;l\u003d394) such that we could in the CommandBuffer do something like:\n\n```\nPerColorAttachment\u003cBindGroupLayoutEntry\u003e bglEntries;\nPerColorAttachment\u003cBindGroupEntry\u003e bgEntries;\nfor each attachment {\n    bglEntries[i].texture.dimension \u003d kInputAttachmentDim;\n    // ...\n}\nDAWN_TRY_ASSIGN(bgl, device-\u003eCreateBGL(...));\nDAWN_TRY_ASSIGN(bg, device-\u003eCreateBG(...));\n\nVkDescriptorSet inputAttachmentSet \u003d ToBackend(bg)-\u003eGetHandle();\n```\n\nThe BindGroupLayout would be cached between submissions like all contentless objects.",
      "revId": "8f08523944a72f57e0c72e6456a231687186a1c6",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
